cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use K-Bound / KGA, please cite it as below."
title: "K-Bound / KGA: Knowability-Guided Adaptation for label-free test-time adaptation"
abstract: >-
  K-Bound formalizes label-free test-time adaptation as an adapt/freeze/abstain
  decision governed by the sign of the adaptation benefit. It contributes an
  impossibility result (the benefit sign is unidentifiable when label-free
  evidence is matched), an exact benefit-sign frontier, and a finite-sample
  certificate (KGA) that controls the false-adapt rate at level alpha. The
  certificate is shipped as the pure-numpy `kga` package.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Niroula
    given-names: Pratik
    email: pratik.niroula.2059@gmail.com
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-26"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Pratikn03/AutoML_Flagship_V8"
keywords:
  - test-time adaptation
  - distribution shift
  - conformal prediction
  - selective prediction
  - safe machine learning
